---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ProjectCaseStudy from '../../components/site/ProjectCaseStudy.astro';
import metadata from '../../siteMetadata';
const project={name:'Roof Ops',context:'Client system',phone:true,logo:'/portfolio/roof-ops-icon.webp',title:'From an AI prototype to a working system.',summary:'Ben had a clear idea and a partly working staff-scoring app he had built with AI. I helped connect the workflow, calculations, supervisor access and deployment so his roofing team could put it to use.',role:'Workflow design · Front-end · Back-end · Authentication · Deployment',status:'Mobile web app · PWA',heroScreens:[{src:'/portfolio/roof-ops-worker.webp',alt:'Roof Ops mobile PWA selecting a client, project, worker and scoring date'},{src:'/portfolio/roof-ops-scoring.webp',alt:'Roof Ops mobile PWA scoring quality, productivity, compliance and teamwork'}],heroCaption:'Choose the worker and project, then capture the scores on a phone.',sections:[
{label:'The starting point',title:'A clear idea. A partly working build.',paragraphs:['Ben and I knew each other from our local coffee shop. He had used AI to prototype daily staff scoring, replacing paper records and helping calculate commission.','A development company was beyond his budget. He had made a start, but staff records, calculations, supervisor access and deployment were keeping him from getting the app into use.']},
{label:'Getting it over the line',title:'Connect the pieces around the real workflow.',paragraphs:['We started with the scoring journey his team needed first. I connected staff records, calculations and supervisor sign-in, working across the interface and back end before deploying the app.','The result was a first release Ben could test with his team. His prototype had helped clarify the idea; putting it into use gave him a practical way to learn what needed to come next.']},
{label:'Mobile scoring',title:'Capture the scores where the work happens.',paragraphs:['The scoring experience runs as a mobile web app, a PWA. Supervisors select the client, project, worker and date before entering scores for quality, productivity, compliance and teamwork.','Large score controls keep the choices visible on a phone. Recent captures give the person recording scores a way to see what they have already entered.'],image:'/portfolio/roof-ops-scoring.webp',alt:'Roof Ops mobile scoring controls from zero to five across four categories',width:782,height:1696,caption:'Four scoring categories, with visible choices sized for the mobile workflow.'},
{label:'Beyond the first release',title:'One system, more of the working day.',paragraphs:['The scoring app led to our next discussion about quality checks, which were spread across paper checklists, phone photos and emails. Ben had to assemble the evidence on his laptop after each job.','I built editable templates for his roofing procedures. Supervisors choose a procedure, complete its checks, attach photos and save a draft before submitting. Checks, photos and notes then form one record for office review and sharing.']},
{label:'The contribution',title:'Make the first idea usable, then build on it.',paragraphs:['My contribution was to help Ben turn his AI-assisted prototype into a usable system, then extend it around the way his business actually works.','Scoring and quality control are parts of the same client system. The work connects what supervisors capture in the field with what the office needs to review and act on.'],links:[{href:'/systems#client-example',label:'Read Ben’s feedback'},{href:'/systems',label:'Explore Workflow Systems'}]}
]};
const pageMetadata={...metadata.defaultMetadata,title:'Roof Ops | James Godwin',description:project.summary,url:metadata.siteUrl+'/work/roof-ops'};
---
<SiteLayout metadata={pageMetadata} current="work"><ProjectCaseStudy project={project}/></SiteLayout>
